@startuml 02b-activity-e2e-pipeline
!include ../_style.iuml
title CMU Sphinx reference: end-to-end ASR pipeline, raw corpus to word error rate

|Corpus preparation|
start
:audio (wav / sph / flac) + transcripts + pronunciation lexicon;
:write etc/<db>_train.fileids + .transcription
and <db>_test.fileids + .transcription
(one utterance per line, "~<s> WORDS ~</s> (fileid)");
:prune lexicon to the words used -> <db>.dic,
derive phone set -> <db>.phone,
noise/silence words -> <db>.filler;
fork
  |Feature extraction|
  :sphinx_fe per utterance (000.comp_feat, or offline)
  pre-emphasis, 25.6 ms Hamming frames every 10 ms,
  FFT, mel filterbank (nfilt, lowerf..upperf),
  log, DCT -> 13 cepstra, lifter 22;
  :write <fileid>.mfc;
fork again
  |Language model|
  :training text, one sentence per line;
  :CMU SLM toolkit or other n-gram tool -> ARPA trigram;
end fork
|Acoustic model training|
:00.verify: dictionary, phones, fileids,
transcripts and features all consistent;
:01/02 LDA + MLLT feature transform (optional);
:10-20 context-independent (CI) HMM, Baum-Welch EM;
:30 untied context-dependent (triphone) HMM;
:40/45 phonetic decision trees, prune to CFG_N_TIED_STATES senones;
:50 tied CD HMM, EM + Gaussian splitting
up to CFG_FINAL_NUM_DENSITIES;
:model_parameters/<db>.cd_cont_<N>/;
|Decoding|
:pocketsphinx_batch over test fileids
(AM + LM + dict + feat.params, DEC_CFG_NPART slices);
:hypotheses -> result/<db>-i-N.match, concatenated to <db>.match;
|Scoring|
:word_align.pl hyp vs reference transcription;
:WER = (S + D + I) / N_ref, SER;
stop
@enduml
